        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dc529da2-4256-575e-8be8-0fee9245161b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Plácido Domingo, Giuseppe Verdi, Francesco Maria Piave, Andrea Maffei, William Shakespeare\n- Works: Repertoire of Plácido Domingo, Macbeth, Ernani, Gianni Schicchi\n- Organizations: Berliner Staatsoper, Metropolitan Opera, Los Angeles Opera\n- Concepts: Opera roles, Debuts, Librettos\n\nFacts:\n- Macbeth is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi.\n- Macbeth has an Italian libretto by Francesco Maria Piave with additions by Andrea Maffei.\n- Macbeth is based on William Shakespeare's play of the same name.\n- Plácido Domingo has officially sung 147 roles in Italian, French, German, English, Spanish, and Russian.\n- In 2015, Plácido Domingo made role debuts as Macbeth at the Berliner Staatsoper, Don Carlo in Ernani at the Metropolitan Opera, and Gianni Schicchi at the Los Angeles Opera.",
